#: source/installation/prerequisites-source.md:1
msgid "Prerequisites"
msgstr ""

#: source/installation/prerequisites-source.md:3
msgid ""
"This list and lower version bounds are maintained on best-effort basis. When "
"in doubt, check the `meson.build` files."
msgstr ""

#: source/installation/prerequisites-source.md:5
msgid "Meson build system (<https://github.com/mesonbuild/meson>)."
msgstr ""

#: source/installation/prerequisites-source.md:7
msgid "Ninja (<https://ninja-build.org/>)."
msgstr ""

#: source/installation/prerequisites-source.md:9
msgid ""
"A version of GCC or Clang that supports C++23 (anything newer than Clang 19 "
"or GCC 14 is likely to work)."
msgstr ""

#: source/installation/prerequisites-source.md:11
msgid ""
"`pkg-config` to locate dependencies. If your distribution does not provide "
"it, you can get it from <http://www.freedesktop.org/wiki/Software/pkg-"
"config>."
msgstr ""

#: source/installation/prerequisites-source.md:14
msgid ""
"The OpenSSL library to calculate cryptographic hashes. If your distribution "
"does not provide it, you can get it from <https://www.openssl.org>."
msgstr ""

#: source/installation/prerequisites-source.md:17
msgid ""
"The `libbrotlienc` and `libbrotlidec` libraries to provide implementation of "
"the Brotli compression algorithm. They are available for download from the "
"official repository <https://github.com/google/brotli>."
msgstr ""

#: source/installation/prerequisites-source.md:20
msgid ""
"cURL library. If your distribution does not provide it, you can get it from "
"<https://curl.haxx.se/>."
msgstr ""

#: source/installation/prerequisites-source.md:23
msgid ""
"The SQLite embedded database library, version 3.6.19 or higher. If your "
"distribution does not provide it, please install it from <http://www.sqlite."
"org/>."
msgstr ""

#: source/installation/prerequisites-source.md:26
msgid ""
"The [Boehm garbage collector (`bdw-gc`)](http://www.hboehm.info/gc/) to "
"reduce the evaluator’s memory consumption (optional). To enable it, install "
"`pkgconfig` and the Boehm garbage collector, and pass the option `-Dlibexpr:"
"gc=enabled` to `meson setup`."
msgstr ""

#: source/installation/prerequisites-source.md:29
msgid ""
"The `boost` library of version 1.87.0 or higher. It can be obtained from the "
"official web site <https://www.boost.org/>."
msgstr ""

#: source/installation/prerequisites-source.md:32
msgid ""
"The `editline` library of version 1.14.0 or higher. It can be obtained from "
"the its repository <https://github.com/troglobit/editline>."
msgstr ""

#: source/installation/prerequisites-source.md:35
msgid ""
"The `libsodium` library for verifying cryptographic signatures of contents "
"fetched from binary caches. It can be obtained from the official web site "
"<https://libsodium.org>."
msgstr ""

#: source/installation/prerequisites-source.md:38
msgid ""
"Recent versions of Bison and Flex to build the parser. (This is because Nix "
"needs C++ template support in Bison and reentrancy support in Flex.)"
msgstr ""

#: source/installation/prerequisites-source.md:41
msgid ""
"The `libseccomp` is used to provide syscall filtering on Linux. This is an "
"optional dependency and can be disabled passing a `-Dlibstore:seccomp-"
"sandboxing=disabled` option to the `meson setup` command (Not recommended "
"unless your system doesn't support `libseccomp`). To get the library, visit "
"<https://github.com/seccomp/libseccomp>."
msgstr ""

#: source/installation/prerequisites-source.md:46
msgid ""
"On 64-bit x86 machines only, `libcpuid` library is used to determine which "
"microarchitecture levels are supported (e.g., as whether to have `x86_64-v2-"
"linux` among additional system types). The library is available from its "
"homepage <http://libcpuid.sourceforge.net>. This is an optional dependency "
"and can be disabled by providing a `-Dlibutil:cpuid=disabled` option to "
"`meson setup` script."
msgstr ""

#: source/installation/prerequisites-source.md:51
msgid ""
"Unless `meson setup build -Dunit-tests=false` is specified, GoogleTest "
"(GTest) and RapidCheck are required, which are available at <https://google."
"github.io/googletest/> and <https://github.com/emil-e/rapidcheck> "
"respectively."
msgstr ""
